    {
      "id": "af4ee4aa",
      "agent_input": "Could you please provide the full text of the Q3 2026 business report for Meridian Analytics? I\u2019d like to review it before saving it for the Executive Team.",
      "agent_response": {
        "response": "Here is the full text of the **Meridian Analytics \u2014 Q3 2026 Business Report** for your review:\n\n---\n\n# Meridian Analytics \u2014 Q3 2026 Business Report\n\n**Period:** July 1 \u2013 September 7, 2026\n**Prepared by:** Rachel Kim, VP of Sales | Claire Fontaine, CFO\n**Distribution:** Executive Team\n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nQ3 2026 marks another strong quarter for Meridian Analytics. Across our 15-person team we closed 14 deals out of 22 opportunities, generating **$1,040,000** in new contract value. The sales pipeline remains healthy with several high-value deals in the pending stage. Customer support ticket volume held steady, with critical issues resolved same-day in all cases.\n\n---\n\n## Sales Performance\n\nTotal closed revenue for the quarter reached **$1,040,000**, with the **South** region leading all territories at **$468,000** in won deals. Our three-person field sales team \u2014 James Okafor, Sofia Delgado, and Marcus Webb \u2014 collectively worked 22 active opportunities during the period.\n\nProduct mix shifted toward Meridian Insights Pro, which accounted for the majority of closed revenue. Meridian DataBridge continues to serve as a strong land-and-expand vehicle with several upsell opportunities maturing in Q4.\n\nWin rate for the quarter stood at **63.6%**, slightly above the company target of 55%. Three deals totalling approximately $240,000 remain in pending status and are expected to close by end of September.\n\n---\n\n## Key Highlights\n\n- **Top deal:** Sofia Delgado closed a $198,000 Meridian Insights Pro contract with a Southern-region enterprise customer on September 5 (D019).\n- **Team headcount:** Meridian Analytics closes Q3 at 15 employees across five departments: Sales (4), Engineering (5), Product (3), HR (1), and Finance (2).\n- **Support SLA:** All critical-priority tickets (TKT-004, TKT-011, TKT-015) were resolved within 24 hours of creation.\n- **License utilisation:** SKU-001 (Meridian Insights Pro) is at 94% capacity \u2014 a procurement review is scheduled for October.\n\n---\n\n## Next Steps\n\n1. Close the three pending deals (D007, D013, D020, D022) before Q3 end.\n2. Begin Q4 pipeline review \u2014 target $1.2M in new ARR.\n3. Resolve the open support tickets (TKT-013, TKT-016, TKT-019) ahead of quarterly customer success calls.\n4. Conduct a license capacity review for SKU-001 and SKU-003 in early October.\n5. HR to initiate two new engineering hire approvals with Kenji Obi to support Q4 roadmap.\n\n---\n\nThat's the complete report. The file is located at `workspace/docs/q3_report.md`. Just let me know when you're ready to save it or if you'd like any edits before distributing it to the Executive Team.",
        "status_code": null
      },
      "from_id": null,
